hub.com/users/gvanrossum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-11-25T05:35:41Z","updated_at":"2015-11-25T05:35:41Z","body":"One bizarre consequence of this is that using six in PY2 code causes a flurry of complaints about the various built-in classes (object, int, etc.). This seems caused by this line in typeshed/third-party/2.7/six/**init**.pyi:\n\n```\nfrom __builtin__ import unichr as unichr\n```\n\nIt finds the **builtin**.pyi stub file but mypy has already read the builtins.pyi stub file and doesn't like the redefinitions. Some sample error messages:\n\n```\n/Users/guido/src/mypy/typeshed/builtins/2.7/__builtin__.pyi: note: In class \"object\":\n/Users/guido/src/mypy/typeshed/builtins/2.7/__builtin__.pyi:31: error: Argument 1 of \"__eq__\" incompatible with supertype \"object\"\n/Users/guido/src/mypy/typeshed/builtins/2.7/__builtin__.pyi:31: error: Return type of \"__eq__\" incompatible with supertype \"object\"\n```\n\n(similar errors are repeated for all methods and classes).\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/159496433/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"gvanrossum","id":2894642,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4OTQ2NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2894642?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum","html_url":"https://github.com/gvanrossum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanros